I've hesitated to report my method of dealing with the wizard before,
because I was afraid that it might be considered a bug, and then fixed
by the development team (may they live long and prosper).  However,
I haven't had much time to devote to Nethack lately so I'll let the
cat out of the bag.  Disclaimer: this works reliably for me on Nethack 
3.0.9 (or 3.0i patchlevel 9 or whatever it was called) but I never 
upgraded to 3.0.10 (or 3.0j or whatever) so it may have been fixed in
that version.  Anyway, when I finally confront the Wizard of Yendor, my 
first hit is to zap him with a wand of cancellation.  Then I slug it out
with him til I kill him.  Needless to say, I never try this until I've
accumulated a lot of hit points (usually > 150), have good armor (< -30),
and a real good weapon (usually blessed +5 Excalibur).  After I kill
him, I retrieve the amulet and polymorph the corpse until I get
somthing tasty and then eat it (after all, I'm not a cannibal).
Using this technique, I've never had the Wiz reincarnate, or come back,
or trouble me again in any fashion.  I'd like to hear from anyone who
tries this with the current patch level.  Does it still work, or not?

